    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Places a form-bound PCF on 11 live model-driven-app forms via solution import + form customization — a host-affecting, hard-to-reverse deploy across a broad matrix; the acceptance is a closed set of 11 named entity forms + an 11-entity smoke pass. ADR-006 (form binding), ADR-026 (Path-A exception), ADR-022 (platform libs verified on the deployed control) bind; UI tests gate the render on representative forms. FULL required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Form-customization + solution import work against Dataverse form definitions for the 11 regarding entities — disjoint from the shared TypeScript (020), the PCF pack (021), and the BFF/schema tracks. It consumes the 021 solution ZIP; it edits no shared source. (Deploy serialization, if any, is an environment concern, not a source-file conflict.)</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-04</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Place the regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` PCF (task 021) on **all 11 regarding-family entity forms** and verify it across the matrix. The 11 entities are exactly those in `RegardingFieldMap.All` (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs`) — READ that file; do NOT hardcode a guessed list:

    1. `sprk_matter` · 2. `sprk_project` · 3. `sprk_invoice` · 4. `sprk_servicerequest` · 5. `sprk_workassignment` · 6. `sprk_event` · 7. `sprk_budget` · 8. `sprk_analysis` · 9. `sprk_organization` · 10. `account` · 11. `contact`

    Requirements (FR-04 all-11):
    - **Place the control on each of the 11 entities' main form** — bind its `anchorField` to that entity's primary Name field, configure the input properties (apiBaseUrl/tenant/clientApp/bffApp per the R1 Timeline PCF config convention), and publish. The control resolves the host record's `(entityType, id)` from context and renders that record's threads-as-groups.
    - **`by-regarding` is entity-set-agnostic** — the endpoint (task 010) inherits R1's impersonation + 2-rule filter and works across all 11 families with flat server cost. The work here is **11 form placements + an 11-entity smoke pass**, NOT 11 endpoints or 11 code variants.
    - **Import the solution ZIP** (from task 021) and do the form customization via the `dataverse-deploy` skill / PAC, OR hand the `pac import` + form-config to the owner if environment auth blocks it (mirror the R1/email-r4 split) — document whichever path is taken. The 11 placements + smoke evidence are the deliverable.
    - **11-entity smoke pass** — confirm the control renders on each of the 11 forms (grouped regarding view, no console errors). UI tests cover ≥2 representative forms in depth (e.g. `sprk_matter` + one non-`sprk_` entity like `contact`); the remaining 9 get a render/no-error smoke check.

    Do NOT modify the PCF code or the shared component here (tasks 020/021) — this task is form placement + config + verification only.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Dataverse deployment engineer fluent in solution import + model-driven-app form customization (adding a code component to a form, binding its `anchorField`, setting input properties, publishing) across many entities, and the `dataverse-deploy` / PAC workflow. Familiar with the 11-entity regarding family (ADR-024) and the R1 Timeline PCF form-config convention.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` PCF is placed on all 11 regarding-family entity forms (the exact set in `RegardingFieldMap.All`), each with `anchorField` bound to that entity's primary Name and input properties configured, published, and verified: an 11-entity smoke pass confirms the grouped regarding view renders on every form with no console errors, with ≥2 representative forms covered in depth by UI tests (incl. an ADR-021 dark-mode check). Placement/import is done via `dataverse-deploy` or handed to the owner (documented). Acceptance is a closed set enumerating the 11 forms.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Surface 1 requires the regarding-mode Timeline on **all 11** regarding-family entity forms from day one (spec Q5 / FR-04). The entity set is authoritative in `RegardingFieldMap.All` — the same map the BFF uses to write typed regarding lookups (ADR-024). Because the `by-regarding` endpoint (task 010) is entity-set-agnostic, there is no per-entity server work; the cost is a flat, broad **form-placement matrix** (spec §High-Risk: "022 — larger deploy/test matrix; server cost is flat, but all 11 forms must be placed + smoke-tested").

      §11 — no new component. This task places the already-built PCF (021) on forms and configures it; it adds no new surface. Cost-of-doing-nothing: without the 11 placements, FR-04's "on all 11 forms" is unmet and Surface 1 exists only on paper. Reuse the R1 Timeline PCF's form-config convention (input-property values, anchor binding).

      Bound `anchorField` (R1 lesson, verified in 021): each placement binds the control to that entity's primary Name field so it appears in the form component library and anchors to the form; the control reads `(entityType, id)` from context. Each of the 11 entities has a primary Name (`sprk_name` for the `sprk_` entities; `account`/`contact` use their OOB primary name — confirm per entity).

      ADR-026 Path-A exception (R1 precedent): the surface is the OOB form + PCF, not a Code Page. Cite in the deploy PR. Access parity (NFR-03) is enforced server-side by the endpoint; nothing on the form re-derives privacy.
    </background>
