  <outputs>
    <output type="config">The regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` PCF placed + configured on all 11 regarding-family entity main forms (anchorField bound to each primary Name; input properties set)</output>
    <output type="docs">11-row smoke matrix (entity → placed → renders → no console errors) + UI-test evidence for the 2 deep forms + any import-vs-owner split (in current-task.md / PR)</output>
  </outputs>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test>`sprk_matter` form (deep): open a Matter with ≥2 threads across ≥2 months; the control renders threads-as-collapsible-groups, expanding a group shows the interleaved email+chat timeline; no console errors.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>`contact` form (deep, non-`sprk_` entity): open a Contact record; the control resolves `(entityType='contact', id)` from context and renders that contact's threads-as-groups — confirming the entity-set-agnostic path works for an OOB entity.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Dark mode (ADR-021): on at least one of the deep forms, switch the model-driven app to dark theme; the grouped view, group headers, and count badges render correctly (Fluent v9 tokens pass through).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>11-entity smoke: opening a record on each of the remaining 9 forms (project, invoice, servicerequest, workassignment, event, budget, analysis, organization, account) renders the control with no console errors.</ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` PCF is placed + form-configured on ALL 11 forms, exactly the set in `RegardingFieldMap.All`: sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_invoice, sprk_servicerequest, sprk_workassignment, sprk_event, sprk_budget, sprk_analysis, sprk_organization, account, contact.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On each of the 11 forms the control's `anchorField` is bound to that entity's primary Name and its input properties (apiBaseUrl/tenant/clientApp/bffApp) are configured; the form is published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The 11-entity smoke pass confirms the grouped regarding view renders on every one of the 11 forms with no console errors (11-row matrix recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UI tests cover ≥2 representative forms in depth (sprk_matter + contact) including an ADR-021 dark-mode check; both resolve the host record's `(entityType, id)` and render threads-as-groups.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No second regarding mechanism, no PCF/shared-code change, and no second endpoint were introduced — form placement + config only (ADR-024, §11); NFR-03 access parity is untouched (nothing on the form re-derives access).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Placement was done via `dataverse-deploy`/PAC, or the `pac import` + form-config was handed to the owner with a runbook — the split is documented; the 11 placements + smoke evidence are recorded either way.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on task 021 (the packed PCF variant). Blocks task 080 (the 11-entity seam-test pass verifies the endpoint side; this task verifies the form side). Because `by-regarding` is entity-set-agnostic, all 11 forms share one control + one endpoint — the risk is purely the breadth of the placement matrix (spec §High-Risk 022), so track a per-entity checklist and do not declare done until all 11 rows pass.

    Confirm the primary Name field per entity: the `sprk_` entities use `sprk_name`; `account` and `contact` use their OOB primary name attributes — bind `anchorField` to the correct one on each form (a wrong binding hides the control from the component library or breaks anchoring).

    If the environment blocks import/auth, split packaging (done in 021) from owner-run import + form-config — hand the owner a per-entity runbook and record which forms the owner still needs to configure.
  </notes>

